1
00:00:02,978 --> 00:00:06,003
And give her a teaspoon of the medicine after every meal.

2
00:00:06,003 --> 00:00:08,020
Don't worry. She'll be fine.

3
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:12,054
You're welcome. Good-bye.

4
00:00:12,054 --> 00:00:25,164
How are you?

5
00:00:25,164 --> 00:00:27,181
I'm tired and hungry.

6
00:00:27,181 --> 00:00:29,198
Well, Marilyn and Richard called.

7
00:00:29,198 --> 00:00:31,215
They'll be here soon, and then we'll eat.

8
00:00:31,215 --> 00:00:34,240
All right. Is...is Susan coming?

9
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:36,257
Well, she'll be here later.

10
00:00:36,257 --> 00:00:38,274
She has to work late tonight.

11
00:00:38,274 --> 00:00:39,282
And what's Robbie cooking for dinner? Robbie

12
00:00:39,282 --> 00:00:42,308
It's a surprise.

13
00:00:42,308 --> 00:00:45,333
I hope it's pasta.

14
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:52,392
Robbie, the dinner was terrific. Robbie

15
00:00:52,392 --> 00:00:54,409
Yes, it was delicious.

16
00:00:54,409 --> 00:00:57,435
What's for dessert?

17
00:00:57,435 --> 00:00:59,452
Oh, I forgot dessert.

18
00:00:59,452 --> 00:01:02,477
Robbie! Robbie

19
00:01:02,477 --> 00:01:03,485
Don't worry.

20
00:01:03,485 --> 00:01:05,502
We've got lots of ice cream.

21
00:01:05,502 --> 00:01:07,519
Oh, I'd love some ice cream.

22
00:01:07,519 --> 00:01:13,570
Well, there's chocolate and coffee and a little vanilla.

23
00:01:13,570 --> 00:01:14,578
I'll have vanilla.

24
00:01:14,578 --> 00:01:16,595
Is that all right with everyone?

25
00:01:16,595 --> 00:01:17,604
I'll have chocolate.

26
00:01:17,604 --> 00:01:19,621
Me, too.

27
00:01:19,621 --> 00:01:22,646
Uh, one scoop of coffee

28
00:01:22,646 --> 00:01:24,663
and one scoop of chocolate for me.

29
00:01:24,663 --> 00:01:28,697
Robbie, will you help me serve? Robbie

30
00:01:28,697 --> 00:01:41,807
I keep thinking about that bag of film. Eight rolls.

31
00:01:41,807 --> 00:01:45,841
A whole day's work.

32
00:01:45,841 --> 00:01:47,858
And good stuff, too.

33
00:01:47,858 --> 00:01:49,874
Don't worry, Richard.

34
00:01:49,874 --> 00:01:50,883
Somenoe will find it.

35
00:01:50,883 --> 00:01:56,934
I'll get it. Hello.

36
00:01:56,934 --> 00:02:03,993
Hello.

37
00:02:03,993 --> 00:02:07,018
Does Richard Stewart live here? Richard Stewart

38
00:02:07,018 --> 00:02:09,035
Yes, he's my brother.

39
00:02:09,035 --> 00:02:11,052
I'm Robbie...Robbie Stewart.

40
00:02:11,052 --> 00:02:14,077
I'm Alexandra Pappas.

41
00:02:14,077 --> 00:02:15,086
How do you do?

42
00:02:15,086 --> 00:02:19,120
Your brother left his bag of film on the ferryboat.

43
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,128
I found it.

44
00:02:20,128 --> 00:02:22,145
I'm really glad to see you.

45
00:02:22,145 --> 00:02:25,170
I mean...my brother'll be really glad to see you!

46
00:02:25,170 --> 00:02:27,187
Robbie! Who is it? Robbie

47
00:02:27,187 --> 00:02:30,213
It's Richard's film! Richard

48
00:02:30,213 --> 00:02:33,238
I mean, Alexandra Pappas.

49
00:02:33,238 --> 00:02:35,255
Come in, please.

50
00:02:35,255 --> 00:02:42,314
Alexandra! Alexandra

51
00:02:42,314 --> 00:02:44,331
Hello, Richard. I found your bag!

52
00:02:44,331 --> 00:02:47,357
Oh, thank you! Thank you!

53
00:02:47,357 --> 00:02:49,373
Um...Alexandra, let me introduce you.

54
00:02:49,373 --> 00:02:51,390
This is my wife Marilyn.

55
00:02:51,390 --> 00:02:53,407
Richard showed me your photo. Richard

56
00:02:53,407 --> 00:02:54,416
How do you do?

57
00:02:54,416 --> 00:02:55,424
Oh yes.

58
00:02:55,424 --> 00:02:56,433
Richard told us all about you. Richard

59
00:02:56,433 --> 00:02:58,450
It's nice to meet you.

60
00:02:58,450 --> 00:03:00,466
And this is my mother, Ellen Stewart.

61
00:03:00,466 --> 00:03:01,475
How do you do?

62
00:03:01,475 --> 00:03:03,492
And my father, Dr. Philip Stewart.

63
00:03:03,492 --> 00:03:05,509
Nice to meet you, Alexandra.

64
00:03:05,509 --> 00:03:06,517
And...ah...you met Robbie.

65
00:03:06,517 --> 00:03:09,543
Yes. And you must be Susan. Hi.

66
00:03:09,543 --> 00:03:11,559
Hi. Welcome.

67
00:03:11,559 --> 00:03:13,576
I'm so glad you found the bag

68
00:03:13,576 --> 00:03:16,602
and took the time and trouble to return it.

69
00:03:16,602 --> 00:03:17,610
Oh, it was no trouble.

70
00:03:17,610 --> 00:03:19,627
I just took the wrong train.

71
00:03:19,627 --> 00:03:21,644
Would you like something to eat?

72
00:03:21,644 --> 00:03:22,653
Thank you, no.

73
00:03:22,653 --> 00:03:24,669
I'm late for dinner at my house.

74
00:03:24,669 --> 00:03:25,678
I really have to go.

75
00:03:25,678 --> 00:03:27,695
Would you like to call home?

76
00:03:27,695 --> 00:03:28,703
I'd appreciate that.

77
00:03:28,703 --> 00:03:30,720
Please, use the phone.

78
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:32,737
Thanks. Excuse me.

79
00:03:32,737 --> 00:03:36,771
Alexandra's a high-school exchange student from Greece. Alexandra

80
00:03:36,771 --> 00:03:37,779
Where does she live?

81
00:03:37,779 --> 00:03:39,796
With a family in the Bronx.

82
00:03:39,796 --> 00:03:41,813
Oh, that's not too far from here!

83
00:03:41,813 --> 00:03:43,830
Take it easy, Robbie.

84
00:03:43,830 --> 00:03:45,847
Thank you.

85
00:03:45,847 --> 00:03:47,864
I can only stay a few minutes.

86
00:03:47,864 --> 00:03:50,889
Have some iced tea.

87
00:03:50,889 --> 00:03:52,906
Thanks, Mrs. Stewart.

88
00:03:52,906 --> 00:03:55,932
Please sit down, Alexandra.

89
00:03:55,932 --> 00:04:05,008
So, you're an exchange student.

90
00:04:05,008 --> 00:04:06,016
Where do you go to school?

91
00:04:06,016 --> 00:04:09,042
At the Bronx High School of Science.

92
00:04:09,042 --> 00:04:11,058
Oh, that's a very good school.

93
00:04:11,058 --> 00:04:13,075
What are your favorite subjects?

94
00:04:13,075 --> 00:04:15,092
Biology and mathematics.

95
00:04:15,092 --> 00:04:17,109
Richard tells me you're a doctor. Richard

96
00:04:17,109 --> 00:04:19,126
Yes, a pediatrician.

97
00:04:19,126 --> 00:04:21,143
And what does your father do?

98
00:04:21,143 --> 00:04:24,168
He's a lawyer, in Thessaloniki.

99
00:04:24,168 --> 00:04:25,177
Would you like some pasta?

100
00:04:25,177 --> 00:04:27,194
I made it myself.

101
00:04:27,194 --> 00:04:28,202
It might be a little cold.

102
00:04:28,202 --> 00:04:33,245
Thanks, no. I do have to go.

103
00:04:33,245 --> 00:04:35,261
It was nice meeting you all.

104
00:04:35,261 --> 00:04:37,278
Well, maybe you'll come for lunch some Sunday,

105
00:04:37,278 --> 00:04:39,295
so we can really thank you

106
00:04:39,295 --> 00:04:40,304
for bringing Richard's bag back.

107
00:04:40,304 --> 00:04:41,312
Maybe.

108
00:04:41,312 --> 00:04:42,321
You're welcome anytime.

109
00:04:42,321 --> 00:04:45,346
Good-bye.

110
00:04:45,346 --> 00:04:52,405
Can I drive you home?

111
00:04:52,405 --> 00:04:53,414
No, thanks.

112
00:04:53,414 --> 00:04:54,422
The train is just up the street.

113
00:04:54,422 --> 00:04:55,431
It won't take me long at all.

114
00:04:55,431 --> 00:04:58,456
Well, you really saved the day for me, Alexandra.

115
00:04:58,456 --> 00:05:00,473
Bye.

116
00:05:00,473 --> 00:05:01,481
Bye-bye.

117
00:05:01,481 --> 00:05:02,490
Good night.

118
00:05:02,490 --> 00:05:13,583
She's a smart young lady, and very nice.

119
00:05:13,583 --> 00:05:17,617
Very! Hey, she forgot her bag!

120
00:05:17,617 --> 00:05:20,642
I guess we'll be seeing Alexandra again.

121
00:05:20,642 --> 00:05:20,642
Right, Robbie?
